troubleshoot:
1. if it shows 'No Container Engine' when open podman, and 'the user has not been granted the requested logon type at this computer' when input 
   'podman machine init' in cmd, that's probably because the virtual machine that images have been built in is dead, need to run 'podman machine init' and 
   'podman machine start' before building the images again.

   note: to make podman work for containers, you need to install podman to create images; to install podman, you need to install wsl

2. podman building images stuck at step 6/7: COPY --chmod=770..
   probably caused by large build contexts or massive node_modules drectories, potential solution: create a .dockerignore file 
   resolved by adding npm cache clean code in dockerfile
   verify: $ curl -v localhost:[port-number]

   note: the difference of curl -v localhost:[port-number] and curl localhost:[port-number] 
   without -v it outputs response body only 'Hello, World!'
   with -v it outputs connection details, request, response headers, response body and connection status
   
3. if it shows 
   'wsl: Nested virtualisation is not supported on this machine.
   Logon failure: the user has not been granted the requested logon type at this computer'
   just run & wsl --shutdown 
   OR:
   $ Get-Service vmcompute | Restart-Service and $ wsl
   then try $ podman machine init and $ podman machine start etc. that should work





